<Song resolves-to="SongSP" spName="PolkadotsandMoonbeams-F-Theme" spTempo="108">
  <spVERSION>4</spVERSION>
  <spComments>Year:	1940
Composer:	Jimmy Van Heusen
Lyricist:	Johnny Burke
Form:	32-bar AABA
Style:	Jazz ballad
Key:	F major

Written by Van Heusen and Burke, the song was
published in 1940 and recorded that year by both the
Glenn Miller and Tommy Dorsey orchestras.
Frank Sinatra’s performance with Dorsey became an
early hit, and the tune later entered the jazz-standard
repertoire. One analysis describes the bridge as a
temporary move from F major to A major.</spComments>
